# ---------- In-scope user intents (exemplars are embedding anchors) ----------
# NOTE: intent names must not contain the reserved Colang keyword "or"; the
# 1.0 parser treats it as a logical operator inside flow references. Prefer
# short neutral names (e.g. "ask programs", not "ask program or degree").
#
# Matching is embeddings-only (config.yml): the user turn is embedded once and
# assigned to the nearest exemplar's intent if it clears the similarity
# threshold, else the fallback intent ("out of scope"). Exemplars are therefore
# nearest-neighbor anchors — breadth across real phrasings matters more than
# volume. These mirror the advertised student questions in frontend/index.html
# and the router capabilities in ChatOrchestrator.

define user ask programs
  "what degrees do you offer"
  "tell me about the nursing program"
  "which certificates can I earn"
  "what are the requirements for the business major"
  "what are the requirements for the computer science degree"
  "tell me about the sociology degree for transfer"
  "does the college have a paralegal certificate"
  "what programs are available at this campus"
  "tell me about the biotechnology certificate"
  "do you have an automotive technology program"
  "what career options does a nursing degree give me"
  "what certifications can I get here"
  "tell me about the business administration transfer degree"
  "do any laccd campuses offer a film program"
  "which colleges in the district have an engineering degree"

